IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsw-wc-core`

-- Workers Compensation Act 1987 (NSW), with the 1998 Act and the 2016 Regulation -- from the seat of the insurer.
--
-- SEAT: the insurer liable on the claim (a licensed insurer, the Nominal Insurer's scheme agent, or a self-insurer). It
-- is a private party, not an official, and the Acts give it hard deadlines with consequences: 7 days from the initial
-- notification to start provisional weekly payments or give notice of a reasonable excuse (1998 Act ss 267, 268), 21 days
-- to determine a claim for weekly payments (s 274, with s 283), the window for a s 48A notice, the work capacity
-- assessments of 1987 Act s 38(4), and the limit on accepting a late claim (1998 Act s 261(5)). "What must I do, by when,
-- and what follows if I don't?" The rules are in nsw-wc-core.l4; this module restates none, and keeps its own names (none
-- shared with nsw-wc-seat.l4 or nsw-wc-seat-employer.l4).
--
-- Edition: the Open Australian Legal Corpus texts as at 10 March 2025 -- not the current official text, and possibly out
-- of date. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation Act 1987 (NSW) -- the insurer's questions`

§§ `After the initial notification of an injury (1998 Act ss 266-269)`

@export What must I do within 7 days of the initial notification of an injury: start provisional weekly payments, or give notice of a reasonable excuse (1998 Act ss 267, 268)?
GIVEN `I have a reasonable excuse the Guidelines recognise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an excuse for not starting provisional weekly payments that the Workers Compensation Guidelines say is a reasonable excuse (s 267(2))
GIVETH A `Duty`
`What must I do within 7 days of the initial notification` MEANS
    `the duty within 7 days of the initial notification` `I have a reasonable excuse the Guidelines recognise`

@export By what day must I start provisional weekly payments, or give the worker written notice of my reasonable excuse (1998 Act ss 267(1), 268)?
GIVEN `the day I was first notified of the injury` IS A DATE @desc The day of the initial notification of the injury to you, in the manner the Guidelines require, by the worker, the employer or someone for either (s 266) (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I act on the initial notification` MEANS
    `the day to act on the initial notification by (1998 Act ss 267(1), 268)` `the day I was first notified of the injury`

§§ `Determining a claim for weekly payments (1998 Act ss 274-276, 283)`

@export By what day must I determine this claim for weekly payments, by accepting liability and starting payments or disputing liability (1998 Act s 274)?
GIVEN `the day the claim for weekly payments was made on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was made (a claim the employer forwarded counts as made on you) (ISO date)
      `the weeks I accepted liability provisionally for` IS A NUMBER @desc If you accepted liability provisionally (s 274(2), or provisional payments under s 267 already running), for how many weeks, up to 12 (0 if not)
      `the day my provisional acceptance began` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it began (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I determine the claim for weekly payments` MEANS
    `the day by which the claim for weekly payments must be determined` `the day the claim for weekly payments was made on me` `the weeks I accepted liability provisionally for` `the day my provisional acceptance began`

@export May I accept liability for weekly payments provisionally for this many weeks (1998 Act s 274(2), (4))?
GIVEN `the weeks I propose` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of weeks of provisional acceptance you propose
      `I was already making provisional payments under Division 1 when the claim was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were already making provisional weekly payments under ss 267-269 when the claim for weekly payments was made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I accept liability provisionally for this many weeks` IF
    `the insurer may accept liability provisionally under s 274(2)` `the weeks I propose` `I was already making provisional payments under Division 1 when the claim was made`

§§ `A late claim (1998 Act s 261(5))`

@export May I determine to accept this late claim (1998 Act s 261(5))?
GIVEN `the day of the injury or death` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened, or for a death claim, the day of the death (ISO date)
      `the day the claimant first became aware of it` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker first became aware of the injury (or the claimant, that the death resulted from it) (ISO date)
      `the day the claim was made on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim was made (ISO date)
      `the Authority approved my accepting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State Insurance Regulatory Authority has approved your accepting it (needed for a claim made more than 3 years after)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I accept this late claim` IF
    `the insurer may determine to accept the late claim`
        (`Claim time facts` WITH
            `the claim is for compensation for a death`                                 IS FALSE  -- placeholder: s 261(5) does not read it
            `the day time runs from`                                                    IS `the day time runs from under s 261(6), (7)` `the day of the injury or death` `the day the claimant first became aware of it`
            `the day the claim was made`                                                IS `the day the claim was made on me`
            `the worker made a claim within time for the injury that caused the death` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: not read
            `the lateness is found to come from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` IS FALSE  -- placeholder: not read
            `the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement`         IS FALSE  -- placeholder: not read
            `the insurer has determined to accept the claim`                            IS FALSE  -- placeholder: not read
            `the Authority approved the insurer's acceptance`                           IS `the Authority approved my accepting it`)

§§ `Return to work notices (1998 Act s 48A)`

@export Is the date I mean to put in a s 48A return to work notice allowed: at least 14 and no more than 60 days after the notice (1998 Act s 48A(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the day I give the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you give the worker the written notice (ISO date)
      `the date I specify` IS A DATE @desc The date from which weekly payments will be suspended unless the worker complies (ISO date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the date in my s 48A notice allowed` IF
    `the date in the s 48A notice is allowed` `the day I give the notice` `the date I specify`

-- Situation: the insurer has given the worker a s 48A(2) notice.
@export I gave the worker a s 48A notice: what may I do now (1998 Act s 48A(3)-(7))?
GIVEN `the day I gave the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the worker the written notice (ISO date)
      `the date I specified` IS A DATE @desc The date the notice specified for the suspension (ISO date)
      `my notice gave the reason, the obligation and the consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice stated the reason, the s 48 obligation the worker must comply with, and the consequences of not complying
      `the worker has complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has complied with the obligation the notice specified
      `the day the worker did so` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the worker complied (otherwise any date)
      `the worker had 2 notices without a suspension, or a suspension, in the 12 months before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the 12 months before this notice, the worker was given 2 such notices with no suspension following, or had weekly payments suspended once
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (ISO date)
GIVETH A `Section 48A answer`
`What may I do now under s 48A` MEANS
    `what the insurer may do under s 48A`
        (`Section 48A facts` WITH
            `the day the notice was given`                                           IS `the day I gave the notice`
            `the date specified in the notice`                                       IS `the date I specified`
            `the notice states the reason, the obligation and the consequences`     IS `my notice gave the reason, the obligation and the consequences`
            `the worker has complied with the obligation in the notice`             IS `the worker has complied`
            `the day the worker complied`                                            IS `the day the worker did so`
            `in the 12 months before the notice: 2 notices without a suspension, or 1 suspension` IS `the worker had 2 notices without a suspension, or a suspension, in the 12 months before`
            `the day asked about`                                                    IS `the day I am asking about`)

§§ `Work capacity assessments (1987 Act s 38(4), (5))`

-- Situation: the worker's second entitlement period (week 130) is ending or has ended.
@export When must I conduct a work capacity assessment of this worker (1987 Act s 38(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the worker's injury has resulted in permanent impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker's injury has resulted in some permanent impairment (s 32A: the start of the test for a worker with highest needs, whom s 38(5) protects)
      `the worker's impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the degree of the worker's permanent impairment has been assessed (under s 65, for Division 4)
      `the worker's assessed degree of impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The assessed degree of whole person impairment, in per cent (0 if not assessed)
      `the worker's assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a medical assessor has declined to assess the worker because maximum medical improvement has not been reached
      `I am satisfied the worker's impairment is likely more than 30%` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, the insurer, are satisfied the worker's degree of permanent impairment is likely to be more than 30%
      `the worker has asked for an assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has asked for a work capacity assessment
      `the last day of the worker's second entitlement period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the worker's second entitlement period (the end of week 130 of weekly payments) (ISO date)
      `I have done one in the last 52 weeks of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already conducted a work capacity assessment during the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period
      `the day of my latest assessment` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day of the latest assessment (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Work capacity assessment answer`
`When must I conduct a work capacity assessment` MEANS
    `the work capacity assessments required` (`is a worker with highest needs` `the worker's impairment facts`) `the worker has asked for an assessment` `the last day of the worker's second entitlement period` `I have done one in the last 52 weeks of that period` `the day of my latest assessment`
    WHERE
        `the worker's impairment facts` MEANS `Impairment facts` WITH
            `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`                             IS `the worker's injury has resulted in permanent impairment`
            `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`                        IS `the worker's impairment has been assessed`
            `the assessed degree of permanent impairment`                                 IS `the worker's assessed degree of impairment`
            `an assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached` IS `the worker's assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached`
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 20%`           IS FALSE  -- placeholder: the highest-needs test does not read it
            `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 30%`           IS `I am satisfied the worker's impairment is likely more than 30%`

§§ `What follows if I miss a duty`

@export What follows if I, the insurer, miss this duty: the maximum penalty, the penalty notice amount, and other consequences?
GIVEN `the insurer's duty` IS A `Duty` @desc The duty: s 267 provisional weekly payments, s 268 notice of a reasonable excuse, or s 274 determining a claim for weekly payments
GIVETH A `Consequence`
`What follows if I, the insurer, miss this duty` MEANS
    `the consequence of missing` `the insurer's duty`
